SUMMARY:Cliffs & Fall Colours: A Bruce Peninsula Hike
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/bruce-peninsula-26)**\n\n*
 *The Bruce Peninsula does dramatic better than almost anywhere else in Ont
 ario\, and fall is when it really shows off.**\n\nWe'll be out for most of
  the day\, covering 8.5km of moderate hiking through some of the best autu
 mn scenery in the province\, with the changing leaves against the escarpme
 nt's limestone making for a proper contrast.\n\nWe'll start in the forest 
 before the trail opens onto the coastline\, tracing the cliffs down to the
  Grotto. It's the most photographed spot on the peninsula for good reason:
  crystal clear water\, a sea cave carved into the rock\, and a natural win
 dow out to the bay. We'll take our time here\, including a stop for lunch.
 \n\nFrom the Grotto we'll keep following the shoreline out to Stormhaven\,
  crossing pebble beaches with open views across Georgian Bay the whole way
 . We'll turn around there and retrace the coastline back\, catching all th
 e same cliffs and colour from the other direction with the light shifted b
 y then.\n\n**Two important things to note:**\n\n1. **Self driving isn't po
 ssible for this trip. Parking passes at the trailhead sell out well in adv
 ance\, so all members travel together on WU transport.**\n2. **Bruce Penin
 sula National Park is stunning\, but be aware that it is a long drive ther
 e and back. Full details are in the itinerary below.**\n\n**Accessibility*
 *\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as
  possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disa
 bility or provide feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wild
 ernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**The Grotto:** The peninsula's most fa
 mous natural feature: a limestone sea cave with turquoise water and a rock
  window looking out over Georgian Bay.\n**Stormhaven Coastline:** A stretc
 h of cobble beach with wide open views across the bay\, well past where mo
 st day hikers turn around.\n**Fall Colour on the Escarpment:** Peak autumn
  colour against the Niagara Escarpment's pale limestone cliffs\, a contras
 t you don't get anywhere else on the Bruce Trail\\*\\*.\\*\\*\n\n**Event c
 ost: $140+HST. Transportation is included in the cost of the adventure. Pl
 ease register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/bruce-pen
 insula-26)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate
  about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changi
 ng magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range 
 from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to To
 ronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't
  reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community m
 embers at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but sm
 all enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [ww
 w.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
